The Stranger (or, as [[Org/Althane/The Weft|the Weft]] have taken to calling him, the Feep) is an entity trapped at the center of [[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]]. He came from [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)/Terminus|Terminus]], the great city on [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)|Syrin]], where he was a media mogul before he became what he is. He is remembered as the one who stole the shard of nothing from the nothing before him.

The route he took out of Syrin left a trail of broken space in the planet's orbit, which [[People/Althane/The Broker|the Broker]] follows to find where he came from. That trail narrows his point of departure to the station that stands over Syrin as [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)/Gilded Spire/index|the Gilded Spire]].

He holds an [[Phenomena/Echo Fragment|Echo Fragment]]. When he took it, the whole of his life was torn out of every record, save for what stands three times removed from him, which might yet be found. [[People/Althane/The Broker|Tech of Sedecium]] holds that the Feep is as he is because he was already so, and that taking the fragment from him, or leaving it, will change nothing in the world. Its true name survives only in the records of [[Org/Omnivox/index|Omnivox]] on [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)|Syrin]], and Tech holds that to learn it would make the Stranger vulnerable.
